| 3a | AT THE MERGE | the house keeps itself (operator, 2026-11-16: //"build it into the house's machina … allow the operator's unlock password to drive the whole thing through the lei caps system"//; design lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep): the house writes an importable carry bundle, its content in clear and its roster of faces sealed to the keep pair (the secret in the bundle's `keep-seat.json` under the steward's passphrase and paper sheet), into an operator-named workspace mirroring a private repo, under a lei the operator's unlock strings; the carry rite keeps the source house's last cut there before the founded house stands. BUILT: `lares rite keep` (its vessel half `rite keep-cut`) lays the bundle into `house/` of the workspace (`house/** -text` in the clone's `.gitattributes`), spends one return of a keep lei the operator strings by hand or by a yes at `vault unlock`, scans for secret-shaped strings, commits, pushes and lands the tessera, and carries this device's sessions under `devices/<name>-<id8>/` in the same commit and push; `--if-due` keeps only a house or sessions that moved, the shim's `down` makes that call, and the wake prints the keep line (`LARES_KEEP_WORKSPACE`, or the one `LARES_WORKSPACES` pair, names the workspace). The operator's env line and a live keep on the founded house BUILT (the first keep pushed `par`). The sealed roster BUILT (PR #259, then PR #270 and the cures of two blind reviews, PR #289): the roster seals to a keep pair whose secret rides the steward's passphrase and paper sheet, each cut signs its manifest, and `config/keep-key` burned; on a pūlama house `pulama keep-seat` writes the seat (PR #287, #290, and #309 on a forced pty), the keep's face derives whoever wears (`515a73bd4`, pinned by PR #303), and a keep meeting its own retired `lar-carry/1` bundle refuses `keep-dest-retired` (PR #314). PARTIAL on the re-stood house (2026-11-19, handoff #/alpha): the operator keeps with `--accept-omissions`, since the face catalog document logs `save-unsealed` at every boot; a full keep waits on that cure. WAITING: the par read that retires `bin/sync` (rank 2a, where `K1`, `K2` and `K11` stand built), with `K5` the root cure after the merge (rank 13c); the keep lei stands one per house, strung by the steward (operator, 2026-11-18, #/rulings), its face derived; the keep's standing design rests at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep. The rite's name stays `keep`: `waiho` names the nihomano binding sigil | The house's memory rests on one disk until it does; the carry rite and the iris/pūlama re-founding both lean on a cut that survives the tear-down. |

